WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.383
Bernoulli equations look almost exactly like

2
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:06.905
linear equations, except for one annoying factor.

3
00:00:06.905 --> 00:00:10.075
y to the n, sitting on the right-hand side.

4
00:00:10.795 --> 00:00:13.769
That y to the n makes the equation nonlinear.

5
00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:17.200
But one substitution, u equals y to the one minus n,

6
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.230
turns it straight back into a linear equation.

7
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.918
And you already know how to solve those.

8
00:00:26.618 --> 00:00:30.408
To spot one, put it in the form your lecture uses.

9
00:00:30.408 --> 00:00:36.436
dy/dx, plus P of x y, equals f of x, times y to the n. Then read off n.

10
00:00:36.856 --> 00:00:39.028
If n is zero, it is just linear.

11
00:00:39.028 --> 00:00:41.048
If n is one, it is separable.

12
00:00:41.048 --> 00:00:43.825
Anything else, that is a Bernoulli equation.

13
00:00:44.245 --> 00:00:48.999
Example from Lecture 5. y prime plus two y equals x y cubed.

14
00:00:48.999 --> 00:00:52.532
Here n is three, so u is y to the minus two.

15
00:00:56.332 --> 00:00:58.716
Here is why the substitution works.

16
00:00:58.716 --> 00:01:02.007
Start by dividing the whole equation by y to the n.

17
00:01:02.427 --> 00:01:05.220
Now let u equal y to the one minus n.

18
00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:11.568
By the chain rule, u prime is one minus n, times y to the minus n, times y prime.

19
00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:16.956
So the first term is u prime over one minus n, and the second term is P u.

20
00:01:16.956 --> 00:01:21.573
Multiply through by one minus n, and you get a linear equation in u.

21
00:01:21.993 --> 00:01:24.668
Your lecture calls this the golden formula.

22
00:01:24.668 --> 00:01:28.307
Memorize it, and you can skip the derivation on the exam.

23
00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:34.479
Now Example 3 from Lecture 5.

24
00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:38.645
x y prime, plus y, equals x squared, y squared.

25
00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:42.236
First, standard form. Divide by x.

26
00:01:42.236 --> 00:01:46.015
y prime, plus one over x y, equals x y squared.

27
00:01:46.015 --> 00:01:49.428
So P is one over x, f is x, and n is two.

28
00:01:49.847 --> 00:01:54.479
Substitute u equals y to the one minus two, which is one over y.

29
00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:56.887
And one minus n is negative one.

30
00:01:57.308 --> 00:01:59.337
Plug into the golden formula.

31
00:01:59.337 --> 00:02:04.411
u prime, minus one over x u, equals negative x. That is linear in u.

32
00:02:04.831 --> 00:02:07.619
The integrating factor is e to the integral of

33
00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:10.770
negative one over x, which is one over x.

34
00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.258
So the derivative of u over x, equals negative one.

35
00:02:15.258 --> 00:02:21.359
Integrate: u over x equals negative x plus C, so u equals C x minus x squared.

36
00:02:21.778 --> 00:02:26.064
Do not stop at u. Back-substitute: y is one over u.

37
00:02:26.064 --> 00:02:29.045
So y equals one over C x minus x squared.

38
00:02:29.466 --> 00:02:30.636
And one more.

39
00:02:30.636 --> 00:02:35.723
y equals zero also solves the original equation, but no value of C gives it.

40
00:02:35.723 --> 00:02:37.244
List it separately.

41
00:02:41.143 --> 00:02:42.635
Three traps from this lecture.

42
00:02:43.056 --> 00:02:46.457
One. Reading off P before standardizing.

43
00:02:46.457 --> 00:02:52.062
For x y prime plus y equals x squared y squared, P is one over x, not one.

44
00:02:52.062 --> 00:02:53.636
Divide by x first.

45
00:02:54.056 --> 00:02:57.761
Two. Multiplying only one side by one minus n.

46
00:02:57.761 --> 00:02:59.923
Both P and f get multiplied.

47
00:03:00.343 --> 00:03:06.111
Three. Leaving the answer in u, or losing y equals zero. The question asked for y.

48
00:03:09.911 --> 00:03:11.175
Here is the recipe.

49
00:03:11.595 --> 00:03:13.818
One. Standard form, and read off n.

50
00:03:14.238 --> 00:03:16.687
Two. Let u equal y to the one minus n.

51
00:03:17.107 --> 00:03:17.743
Three.

52
00:03:17.743 --> 00:03:22.243
Use the golden formula, and solve the linear equation with an integrating factor.

53
00:03:22.663 --> 00:03:27.158
Four. Go back to y, and check whether y equals zero is a solution.

54
00:03:27.578 --> 00:03:32.791
Next up, homogeneous equations, where everything depends only on y over x.
